billions of people around the world  planning to ring in the New Year tonight  [Applause]  it is already 2019 in places like  Auckland New Zealand thousands of people  celebrated with a party and fireworks in  that western Pacific City here in New  York more than a million people are  expected to pack into Times Square  roughly seven thousand police officers  and heavily armed counterterrorism teams  will stand by to keep them safe and for  the first time this year a high-flying  security measure will watch from the sky  Tony Duke opal is in Time Square Tony  tell us all about it  oh good morning good morning this will  be the heart of the crowd in just about  12 hours that if you look over my  shoulder the ball drop is right there  let me give you an idea of the security  these barricades went up overnight all  the trash cans in this area have been  removed protectively and the NYPD has  even gone so far as to seal the manhole  covers under our feet in this area all  that plus an on-duty force tonight  described to me as larger than the  police force of most major cities any  night of the year  for the New York Police Department  preparing for New Year's Eve is a  year-long affair when midnight strikes  the ball drops and everybody goes home  we start planning for next year John  Miller is the NYPD's Deputy Commissioner  for intelligence and counterterrorism he  says people hoping to celebrate here  tonight will go through metal detectors  first no backpacks coolers or umbrellas  will be allowed some people may even be  patted down if officers feel there is  something they need to take a closer  look at it's not quite like going to the  airport because we've got to move it  through but it has some of the same  elements there will be plenty of police  presence  many wearing tactical gear and armed  with high-capacity weapons others will  blend in with the crowd on rooftops  snipers plus officers embedded inside  surrounding hotels so that if you have  something that occurs in a hotel either  before the event or during the event you  don't have to figure out well which  hotel is it how are we going to get  people there all of that built in like  last year more than 200 police cars and  sanitation trucks will block roadways to  prevent a car from driving into the  crowds but this year the NYPD will have  an additional set of eyes in the sky for  the first time an NYPD drone will be  part of the aerial arsenal  it's designed to supplement police  helicopters circling above and the more  than 1,200 fixed cameras in the ten  block area below how does a drone fit  into the overall plan the drone actually  is able to give us a view inside any of  the gaps between those cameras it gives  us flexibility visibility and agility  that you wouldn't have with another  device now important to point out that  police say there is no specific credible  threat to the celebration tonight but  according to Deputy Commissioner Miller  the NYPD has foiled roughly 30 terror  plots since 9/11 and their guard is  always up I asked him what he would say  to somebody who is worried nonetheless  and he said this is the safest place to  be in New York tonight and Anthony he  even brings his own kids they do an  amazing job Tony thank you
 

